course: dictionary
lesson: 5150
title: One word, four meanings: iron
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Iron can be a metal, a tool, a verb or a describing word. The words around it tell you which one you need. «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster» is about the metal, because only metal can rust. «To iron clothes» is a verb, because it is something you do.
explain: Check the clues before you choose. «Blood tests can check things like iron» is about the mineral in your blood, because blood tests look inside your body. «The old iron gate creaked» uses iron to describe the gate, so it works like a describing word. Ask: what does iron do, or what is it?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If you think «The outer core is liquid iron and nickel» means a tool, put the tool meaning in: a liquid tool and nickel does not make sense. So it must mean the metal. Swapping in a meaning is a quick check you can use with any word.
fact: Iron is a strong, hard, grey metal used to make steel, tools, gates and railings.
fact: An iron is a household tool with a flat hot bottom that you press on clothes to make them smooth. To iron clothes means to smooth them with an iron.
fact: Iron is also a mineral your body needs in its blood. Spinach, red meat and beans contain iron.
fact: Iron is magnetic, so magnets attract it. It rusts when it is wet and in air.
fact: «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide, the same kind of substance as rust.»
exercise: «Iron the shirt before school, please.» What does iron mean here? | To hit something very hard | *To make clothes smooth with a hot, flat tool | To lock a gate with a metal bar | To carry a heavy load up a hill
exercise: «The outer core is liquid iron and nickel.» What kind of word is iron here? | *A noun for a metal | A name for a tool that is hot | A verb meaning to smooth | A describing word for a gate
exercise: «The old iron gate creaked.» What is iron doing in this sentence? | Naming a blood mineral | *Describing the gate, so it is made of iron | Naming a household tool | Telling you to press something
test: «Blood tests can check things like iron.» In this sentence, iron means | *A mineral that your blood needs | A flat hot tool for clothes | A grey paint for fences | A type of rain
test: Why does «Mars look red»? Read the sentence: «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide.» | Its dust is the colour of spinach | *Its dust contains iron oxide, the same kind of substance as rust | It is painted by the Sun | Its dust is made of hot clothes
exam: Which statement about iron is true? | Iron never rusts, even when it is wet | Iron is a food you eat with milk | Iron is the name for a hot flat tool only | *Magnets attract iron
